  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The left side of the second equation is \\(-2(2x-3y).\\) If the first equation holds, that expression must equal \\(-2\\cdot8=-16,\\) but the second equation says it equals \\(9.\\) This contradiction means that no ordered pair satisfies both equations.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare the left side of the second equation with the left side of the first",
        "Multiplying the first equation by \\(-2\\) would require the second right side to be \\(-16\\)"
      ],
